  "verdict": "The filled twin occupies the same visual extent as the outlined one in 94% of pairs, to within 0.01 units, so the keylines, the 2-unit clearance and the centring rules carry over unchanged and the \"filled icons run larger\" reading is an artefact of comparing a filled bbox against an outlined path bbox rather than against its visual extent. What does not carry over is everything about interior white: 932 of 2,085 icons knock a hole out of a solid, and no primitive can express that. Corner radii move: only 43% of filled corners land on the house tiers, because the dominant corner is the outlined tier plus half a stroke. 63% of filled solids are neither a disc nor an axis-aligned rounded rect, so a generator restricted to rect/circle/line/dot/part reaches a minority of this set however the knockout question is answered. 107 icons ship a solid buried inside another solid of a different element, where the fill rule cannot reach it and both paint currentColor — geometry that draws nothing. That is the set being inconsistent, not a rule to copy."
